    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 66.89 efficiency rating. While he faces a slight dynamic platoon disadvantage against the left-handed Prielipp, the combination of his top-tier raw projection and the high-leverage 3-hole batting position makes him our primary anchor. **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Brice Turang** also present strong profiles, with **Tyler Soderstrom** benefiting significantly from a +10% park factor adjustment, while **Brice Turang** leverages a favorable spot in the order to secure a 62.96 score. **Travis Bazzana** rounds out our top-tier plays; despite a modest base projection, his role as the leadoff hitter against Imai\u2019s pedestrian 4.82 xERA makes him a high-upside play for run production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the roster involves **Austin Riley**, who sits at a marginal 44.97 due to a challenging matchup against Misiorowski. He remains in the lineup solely for his floor, though he was nearly displaced by **Cole Young**, whose 40.23 score fell just short. **Cole Young** was under consideration due to the scarcity of stolen bases, but the optimizer ultimately prioritized **Austin Riley**\u2019s plate appearances to avoid burning a game cap on a lower-floor asset. Elsewhere, **Seiya Suzuki** is a calculated risk; while his base projection is solid, the matchup against Gausman suppresses his ceiling, though his speed profile against a deliberate delivery keeps him in the starting nine as a potential thief. \n\nManagers should remain vigilant regarding the matchup between **Gabriel Moreno** and Prielipp. While the 56.10 score is viable, the platoon disadvantage against a southpaw keeps expectations tempered. We are also monitoring the remaining bench closely; **Jose Caballero** remains sidelined, and our long-term injury concerns regarding **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story** continue to compress our active roster depth. With **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Henry Bolte** also unavailable or sitting for rotation purposes, the current active lineup represents our highest probability for efficiency across all five categories, particularly our focus on SB output.",
